{"slug":"course-schedule","title":"Course Schedule","level":"Medium","summary":"prerequisites[i] = [a, b] means take b before a. Return whether all numCourses courses can be finished.","method":"canFinish","params":[["int","numCourses"],["int[][]","prerequisites"]],"returns":"boolean","tests":[{"in":["2","[[1,0]]"],"out":"true"},{"in":["2","[[1,0],[0,1]]"],"out":"false"},{"in":["1","[]"],"out":"true"},{"in":["4","[[1,0],[2,1],[3,2],[1,3]]"],"out":"false"},{"in":["5","[[1,4],[2,4],[3,1],[3,2]]"],"out":"true"}],"lesson":"topological-sort","anchor":"course-schedule--can-you-finish"},
{"slug":"course-schedule-ii","title":"Course Schedule II","level":"Medium","summary":"Return any order in which all courses can be taken given the prerequisite pairs [a, b] (b first), or an empty array if impossible.","method":"findOrder","params":[["int","numCourses"],["int[][]","prerequisites"]],"returns":"int[]","check":"custom:topoOrder","tests":[{"in":["2","[[1,0]]"],"out":"[0,1]"},{"in":["4","[[1,0],[2,0],[3,1],[3,2]]"],"out":"[0,1,2,3]"},{"in":["1","[]"],"out":"[0]"},{"in":["2","[[0,1],[1,0]]"],"out":"[]"},{"in":["6","[[5,4],[4,3],[3,2],[2,1],[1,0]]"],"out":"[0,1,2,3,4,5]"}],"lesson":"topological-sort"},
{"slug":"course-schedule-iv","title":"Course Schedule IV","level":"Medium","summary":"Given direct prerequisites [a, b] (a before b), answer each query [u, v]: is u a prerequisite of v, directly or indirectly?","method":"checkIfPrerequisite","params":[["int","numCourses"],["int[][]","prerequisites"],["int[][]","queries"]],"returns":"List<Boolean>","tests":[{"in":["2","[[1,0]]","[[0,1],[1,0]]"],"out":"[false,true]"},{"in":["2","[]","[[1,0],[0,1]]"],"out":"[false,false]"},{"in":["3","[[1,2],[1,0],[2,0]]","[[1,0],[1,2]]"],"out":"[true,true]"},{"in":["4","[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3]]","[[0,3],[3,0],[1,3]]"],"out":"[true,false,true]"}],"lesson":"topological-sort"},
{"slug":"minimum-height-trees","title":"Minimum Height Trees","level":"Medium","summary":"An undirected tree has n nodes. Return every node that, used as the root, gives the minimum possible height. Any order.","method":"findMinHeightTrees","params":[["int","n"],["int[][]","edges"]],"returns":"List<Integer>","check":"any-order","tests":[{"in":["4","[[1,0],[1,2],[1,3]]"],"out":"[1]"},{"in":["6","[[3,0],[3,1],[3,2],[3,4],[5,4]]"],"out":"[3,4]"},{"in":["1","[]"],"out":"[0]"},{"in":["2","[[0,1]]"],"out":"[0,1]"},{"in":["7","[[0,1],[1,2],[1,3],[2,4],[3,5],[4,6]]"],"out":"[1,2]"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#5:d4d01b12bb95d960\"","perf":{"label":"a tree of 20,000 nodes","gen":"int a0 = 20000; int[][] a1 = BCB.treeEdges(20000, 0);"},"refMs":13}],"lesson":"topological-sort"},
{"slug":"find-eventual-safe-states","title":"Find Eventual Safe States","level":"Medium","summary":"In a directed graph (graph[i] lists i's targets), a node is safe if every path from it ends at a node with no outgoing edges. Return all safe nodes in ascending order.","method":"eventualSafeNodes","params":[["int[][]","graph"]],"returns":"List<Integer>","tests":[{"in":["[[1,2],[2,3],[5],[0],[5],[],[]]"],"out":"[2,4,5,6]"},{"in":["[[1,2,3,4],[1,2],[3,4],[0,4],[]]"],"out":"[4]"},{"in":["[[]]"],"out":"[0]"},{"in":["[[0]]"],"out":"[]"},{"in":["[[1],[2],[]]"],"out":"[0,1,2]"},{"in":[],"out":"\"#14152:254caf08da8de3f7\"","perf":{"label":"10,000 nodes","gen":"int n = 10000; int[][] a0 = new int[n][]; for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) { TreeSet<Integer> ts = new TreeSet<>(); int deg = BCB.rnd(0, 4); while (ts.size() < deg) ts.add(BCB.rnd(0, n - 1)); a0[i] = ts.stream().mapToInt(x -> x).toArray(); }"},"refMs":1}],"lesson":"topological-sort"},
{"slug":"find-all-possible-recipes-from-given-supplies","title":"Find All Possible Recipes from Given Supplies","level":"Medium","summary":"Recipe i needs every item in ingredients[i]; ingredients can be supplies (unlimited) or other recipes. Return every recipe you can make, in any order.","method":"findAllRecipes","params":[["String[]","recipes"],["List<List<String>>","ingredients"],["String[]","supplies"]],"returns":"List<String>","check":"any-order","tests":[{"in":["[\"bread\"]","[[\"yeast\",\"flour\"]]","[\"yeast\",\"flour\",\"corn\"]"],"out":"[\"bread\"]"},{"in":["[\"bread\",\"sandwich\"]","[[\"yeast\",\"flour\"],[\"bread\",\"meat\"]]","[\"yeast\",\"flour\",\"meat\"]"],"out":"[\"bread\",\"sandwich\"]"},{"in":["[\"bread\",\"sandwich\",\"burger\"]","[[\"yeast\",\"flour\"],[\"bread\",\"meat\"],[\"sandwich\",\"meat\",\"bread\"]]","[\"yeast\",\"flour\",\"meat\"]"],"out":"[\"bread\",\"sandwich\",\"burger\"]"},{"in":["[\"a\",\"b\"]","[[\"b\"],[\"a\"]]","[\"x\"]"],"out":"[]"}],"lesson":"topological-sort"},
{"slug":"sort-items-by-groups-respecting-dependencies","title":"Sort Items by Groups Respecting Dependencies","level":"Hard","summary":"Order n items so that items of the same group are next to each other and every item comes after all items in beforeItems[i]. group[i] = -1 means no group. Return any valid order, or [] if none exists.","method":"sortItems","params":[["int","n"],["int","m"],["int[]","group"],["List<List<Integer>>","beforeItems"]],"returns":"int[]","check":"custom:sortItems","tests":[{"in":["8","2","[-1,-1,1,0,0,1,0,-1]","[[],[6],[5],[6],[3,6],[],[],[]]"],"out":"[6,3,4,5,2,0,7,1]"},{"in":["8","2","[-1,-1,1,0,0,1,0,-1]","[[],[6],[5],[6],[3],[],[4],[]]"],"out":"[]"},{"in":["1","1","[-1]","[[]]"],"out":"[0]"},{"in":["3","1","[0,-1,0]","[[],[0],[1]]"],"out":"[]"}],"lesson":"topological-sort"}
